            "After discharge, transfer or death, the room is cleaned <strong>before the next patient</strong>, by cleaners briefed on the organism and wearing gloves and apron (plus mask for airborne organisms until the room has been ventilated — leave an airborne room empty with windows open for an hour, or longer where air changes are poor).",
            "<strong>Remove</strong> all disposable items, linen (into the infected stream) and waste; <strong>discard</strong> opened consumables, lotions and soaps; <strong>decontaminate</strong> dedicated equipment (cuff, stethoscope, commode, pump) before it returns to general use.",
